{% comment %}
  owv2 buy panel. Restyles vendor mechanics; adds no cart logic of its own —
  `product-info.js` (variant resolution) and `product-form.js` (add-to-cart)
  own that, via the vendor snippets rendered below.

  Requires: `product`. Reads `section` implicitly (global object; see the
  vendor `product-variant-options.liquid`, which does the same without
  receiving it as a render argument).

  --- Step 1: vendor interface capture (Task 4) ---

  `product-variant-picker.liquid` reads: block.settings.picker_type,
  block.settings.swatch_type, block.settings.swatch_source,
  block.settings.show_variant_labels, block.settings.size_chart,
  block.settings.enable_swatch_unavailable_click (via the
  product-variant-options partial it renders), plus block.id and
  block.shopify_attributes.

  `buy-buttons.liquid` reads: block.settings.show_gift_card_recipient,
  block.settings.show_dynamic_checkout, block.settings.show_quantity_selector,
  plus block.id and block.shopify_attributes.

  Decision: path (a). Liquid has no object-literal syntax, so a
  `{% capture %}`/`{% assign %}` stand-in can only ever be a string or a
  blank/nil value — it cannot expose `.settings.picker_type` style dotted
  reads the way a real block does. A nil `block` would silently degrade
  every one of the reads above (nil.settings.x is nil, not an error) but
  would also mean no picker_type: 'button' pill styling, no swatch config,
  and empty block.shopify_attributes/block.id everywhere — invisible to
  theme check but wrong at runtime. So `owv2-product-main`'s schema declares
  `variant_picker` and `buy_buttons` theme blocks that mirror
  `sections/main-product.liquid`'s block definitions field-for-field
  (including its `t:sections.main-product.blocks.*` translation keys, which
  already exist in the locale files), and this snippet renders the vendor
  snippets against `section.blocks | where: 'type', '<type>' | first`. That
  gives both vendor snippets a real block object — correct settings, working
  `block.id`, working `block.shopify_attributes` — the same shape
  `main-product.liquid:797,801` passes them. The Subscriptions `@app` block
  is declared alongside them in the same schema but is placed by the theme
  editor in the template JSON (Task 7), never rendered here — see the loop
  below.

  Two schema defaults deliberately diverge from `main-product`'s block
  (both restyle-scope choices, not vendor-interface changes): `swatch_type`
  defaults to `none` (no swatch CSS has shipped for this panel yet — see
  Step 3's pill selectors) and `show_dynamic_checkout` defaults to `false`
  (the vendor `payment_button` renders its own unstyled UI outside the pill
  system). Both are ordinary theme-editor settings a merchant can change.
{% endcomment %}
{%- assign product_form_id = 'product-form-' | append: section.id -%}
{%- assign variant_picker_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'variant_picker' | first -%}
{%- assign buy_buttons_block = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'buy_buttons' | first -%}
<div class="pdp-buy">
  <div class="pdp-price" aria-live="polite">
    <span class="pdp-price__now" data-price>{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price | money }}</span>
    <s class="pdp-price__was" data-compare-at
      {%- unless product.selected_or_first_available_variant.compare_at_price > product.selected_or_first_available_variant.price %} hidden{% endunless %}>
      {{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.compare_at_price | money }}
    </s>
  </div>

  {% render 'product-variant-picker', block: variant_picker_block, product: product, product_form_id: product_form_id %}

  {%- comment -%}
    Subscribe / one-time: the Shopify Subscriptions app block. An
    `shopify://apps/...` block can't be `{% render %}`d from a snippet — it
    is placed in the template JSON (Task 7) as an `@app` block on this
    section, and rendered wherever the merchant drags it via the loop below.
    No selling plan on the product → nothing extra needs to render; the
    buy-buttons below already handle plain add-to-cart.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}
      {% render block %}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {% render 'buy-buttons', block: buy_buttons_block, product: product, section_id: section.id, product_form_id: product_form_id, show_pickup_availability: false %}
</div>
